WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.589
The Mandalorian has proven itself to not only
be one of the best original offerings on Disney+,

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:08.300
but one of the best new shows on television,
period.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.929
Its conflicted protagonist is a member of
a dying race, a warlike yet honorable people

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:16.830
who once inhabited the planet Mandalore in
the time of the Old Republic.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.330
During the time period in which the series
is set, in between the original and sequel

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.220
film trilogies, they're a people whose numbers
are dwindling fast, due to a long, long history

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.480
of conflict that has led them to being forsaken
by their own government and exiled to the

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.660
moon of Concordia, where they were left to
die out.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.809
While the history of Mandalore is a bit fluid,
one thing that has never changed is the race's

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:41.320
distinctive armor, armor which has been very
familiar to fans ever since the first big-screen

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.519
appearance of the bounty hunter Boba Fett
in Star Wars Episode V: The Empire Strikes

00:00:45.519 --> 00:00:46.570
Back.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.309
Before the release of The Mandalorian, it
was even speculated by some fans that the

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:55.050
title character might actually be Boba Fett,
as that character's fate has been retconned

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:59.469
since his seemingly fatal plunge into the
Sarlacc pit in Star Wars Episode VI: Return

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:00.469
of the Jedi.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:04.700
It turns out that Boba is still alive, meaning
that he may very well be wandering the galaxy

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.390
during the events of The Mandalorian, but
the differences between the two characters

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.890
are many, and significant.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.860
All of these differences stem from the most
obvious one: Boba Fett isn't actually Mandalorian.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.300
He's a clone of Jango Fett, who claimed to
hail from Concord Dawn, a planet within the

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.800
Mandalore system.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.790
Although Jango wore Mandalorian armor outfitted
with the types of bells and whistles common

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:30.110
to those worn by the warrior race, he had
been disavowed by the Mandalorian government,

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.420
which regarded him as nothing more than a
scoundrel, a common mercenary whose only interest

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.910
was in a paycheck.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:40.140
This goes to the core of the differences between
Boba Fett, who followed in his father's footsteps

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.970
in becoming the most feared bounty hunter
in the galaxy, and the Mandalorian, whose

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.610
identity is very strongly tied to his homeworld
and its culture.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.610
"What caused this damage?"

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.110
"A Mudhorn."

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.560
"Then you have earned the Mudhorn as your
signit.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.950
I shall craft it."

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:02.360
While both Boba and the Mandalorian are seen
operating as bounty hunters, and both operate

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.880
mostly according to the codes of that profession,
that and their armor is basically where the

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.610
similarities end.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:13.049
This is because, like his father before him,
Boba Fett's code of honor is largely his own,

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:17.930
untethered to any larger philosophy, which
stands in stark contrast to the Mandalorian,

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:21.760
whose code isn't just a personal preference,
but his actual religion.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.719
In the series' second episode, the titular
Mandalorian states explicitly: "I'm a Mandalorian.

00:02:26.719 --> 00:02:28.060
Weapons are part of my religion."

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:33.249
So, too, is Beskar steel, the substance from
which much of the Mandalorian's armor is forged,

00:02:33.249 --> 00:02:36.969
and which is considered by members of his
race to be a religious sacrament.

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:42.159
Boba Fett, by contrast, has no such spiritual
connection to Beskar, his weapons, or Mandalorian

00:02:42.159 --> 00:02:43.159
culture.

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:47.670
His use of Mandalorian armor and tactics is
largely an accident; his father had used his

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:52.639
loose, if even existent, connection to Mandalore
to bolster his own reputation, and indeed,

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:57.489
his use of Manadlorian armor was quite effective
in striking fear into the hearts of his quarry.

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:00.730
According to Boba Fett's backstory, though,
the bounty hunter essentially wore the armor

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.980
because his father did.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.980
What.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.120
A. Daddy's boy.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.999
One could certainly make the case that the
Mandalorian's connection to his dying culture

00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:12.139
and the ways of Mandalore make him a far more
interesting character than Boba Fett ever

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:13.139
was.

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:16.480
They may both be a couple of bounty hunters
in cool armor perpetually on the hunt for

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.560
their next job, but the Mandalorian's reaction
to the sticky situation in which he finds

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.889
himself after taking custody of Baby Yoda
is informed by more than his need for a payday.

00:03:25.889 --> 00:03:30.220
It's informed by the strong sense of honor
which is typical of all Mandalorians, and

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:34.599
it's even safe to say that if Boba Fett had
found himself in the same situation, he might

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:39.310
have decided to save himself a major hassle
by simply terminating his green, cuddly target,

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.409
and settling for the slightly smaller fee.

00:03:41.409 --> 00:03:42.409
"Bounty hunters!

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:45.389
We don't need their scum."

